/T (Unmanned aerial vehicle navigation spoofing equipment is a standardized product that meets the  Electric Power System Safety Anti-terrorism Protection Requirements' and the  Petroleum and Petrochemical System Safety Anti-terrorism Protection Requirements'. By transmitting low-power retransmitted satellite signals, it intrudes into the  black flight' unmanned aerial vehicle navigation system, thereby achieving  interception control of drones that require satellite navigation systems for flight  control, preventing them from flying into protected areas and ensuringlow-altitude safety in those areas. The product is rigorously designed and produced according to civilian radio frequency products. In [year], it was inspected by the National Radio Frequency Testing Center and obtained the corresponding test  report, and in [year], it obtained the first batch of model approval codes from the  Ministry of Industry and Information Technology for this type of product.)
