/Title (The manned-unmanned integrated detection and countermeasure equipment is a new type of unmanned detection and countermeasure device mainly developed for security threats caused by unmanned aerial vehicles \(UAVs\), targeting mainly public security and military personnel. The equipment consists of three parts: the unmanned detection positioning module, the unmanned interference interception module, and the unmanned navigation decoy module. The unmanned detection positioning module can analyze communication link signals between the UAV and the remote controller to obtain various data information such as the UAV's unique serial number, model, position, altitude, speed, elevation, heading, departure point, return point, pilot position, and more.Combined with our company's platform software, the location of drones, pilots, flight direction, and trajectories can be plotted on a map for quick positioning and tracking of unmanned aerial vehicles \(UAVs\) and pilots. At the same time, a drone disturbance block can be activated to cut off communication links between UAVs or cross-planes and remote controllers, rendering UAV pilots unable to control their UAVs. The drone navigation spoofing block can also be combined with UAV guidance to implement tactical functions such as forced landing, directed expulsion, and targeted deception in no-fly zones.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3135 0 R
/Next 3157 0 R
>>
